From ec62761486b74b974314c2c6cd5e46a025eb6bde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HaoWang113 <18701975378@163.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 17:38:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [ckpt, rollout] fix: ship the delta seed as full-coverage
 indices flushes

The seed (first sync) streamed the full export over the values-only wire
(wire tag "dense"), which lands on the receiver's vLLM layerwise-reload
path. That machinery copies reloaded values back into the original
parameter storage assuming runtime layout == checkpoint layout; Ascend
fused-expert weights violate that after vllm-ascend's
process_weights_after_loading transpose(1, 2), so the very first sync
crashed in aclnnInplaceCopy on NPU MoE rollouts ([128, 2N, K] copied
into [128, K, 2N]) before any sparse session could open.

- delta_sync/pipeline.py: _send_full_seed now dispatches; the seed ships
  as full-coverage indices flushes through the existing steady assembly
  (_bucket_full_coverage + _assemble_flush + _publish_flush), so every
  seed write goes through the receiver's verl-owned layout window. The
  SGLang verify sweep keeps the values-only wire (_send_values_sweep).
  Wire cost ~3x the values seed (int32 positions + values), paid once
  per engine start.
- delta_weight_transfer.py: fail loud when a dense flush arrives and the
  rollout model has fused-expert modules -- the dense path is
  structurally broken there; point operators at the indices seed.

The NCCL/CUDA delta engine shares this mixin and switches identically
(uniform protocol; its MoE dense seed worked only by layout coincidence).

Co-authored-by: GLM5.3 <noreply@zhipuai.com>
Signed-off-by: Hao Wang <wanghao232@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Chuan Zheng <zhengchuan@huawei.com>
